1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,771
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,362
[reporter] <i>Diego Torillo has the lead</i>

6
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:32,323
<i>over Congressman Julio Ardiente</i>
<i>in the election.</i>

7
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,785
[people shouting]

8
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:39,247
<i>The Ardientes always win.</i>

9
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:40,832
<i>Julio Ardiente's winning.</i>

10
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:41,916
-<i>Huh?</i>
-<i>What?</i>

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,084
[Emilia screams]

12
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:45,628
<i>You're going to have us killed, huh?</i>

13
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:46,463
<i>In your dreams!</i>

14
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:50,091
[Julio] <i>My grandson, victory is yours.</i>

15
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:54,471
-<i>Tell me who should pay.</i>
-[Arnaldo groans]

16
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:56,556
[Ivy] <i>How long will he stay like this?</i>

17
00:00:56,639 --> 00:00:58,975
<i>It might take him months</i>
<i>before he can fully recover</i>

18
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:01,061
<i>and regain all his memory back.</i>

19
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:04,814
[Ivy] <i>Governor Julio Ardiente,</i>
<i>congratulations.</i>

20
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:07,317
<i>Your new title suits you.</i>

21
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:11,821
[Julio] <i>My enemies should start</i>
<i>saying their prayers</i>

22
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:14,657
<i>because this is</i>
<i>the beginning of their end.</i>

23
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:19,454
[Diego] <i>So Julio Ardiente, I am</i>
<i>challenging you to a recount,</i>

24
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:24,459
<i>to find out who the people</i>
<i>of this province voted for!</i>

25
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:27,462
[crowd chanting]
<i>Julio Ardiente is a cheater!</i>

26
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:30,465
<i>Julio Ardiente is a cheater!</i>

27
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:32,675
[Ivy] <i>Tell your men to stop this!</i>

28
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,677
[Julio] <i>Who are you to give me orders?</i>

29
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:36,763
<i>No one tells me what to do.</i>

30
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:40,600
<i>You need me more than I need you!</i>

31
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:43,228
[Emilia] <i>An Ardiente never loses.</i>

32
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:46,606
<i>I will always be an Ardiente.</i>

33
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:50,235
<i>I will rise up and destroy you all.</i>

34
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:53,029
[Julio] Cheers!

35
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:55,990
Thank you very much for your support.

36
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:57,450
[woman] Congratulations.

37
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,578
Thank you very much.

38
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:04,415
[Ivy] <i>Your actions make</i>
<i>my skin crawl, Julio.</i>

39
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:07,168
<i>I know you were just testing me.</i>

40
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:10,004
[indistinct chatter]

41
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:13,216
<i>But the next time you do it,</i>

42
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:17,178
<i>I'll make sure you'll regret it.</i>

43
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:20,515
[tense music plays]

44
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:24,477
[indistinct chatter]

45
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:27,230
Thank you, everyone.

46
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:34,696
[Fernan] Diego.

47
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:38,324
Julio's men raided our homes…

48
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:40,994
-and stole all our belongings.
-[somber music playing]

49
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:44,914
Mister Fernan, we'll get back
what they stole.

50
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:46,416
Don't worry.

51
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:54,632
Mister Danny, are you okay?

52
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:55,967
-Yeah.
-Does it hurt?

53
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,468
-It does.
-Diego.

54
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:59,178
-Diego.
-Diego.

55
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:01,514
-Nanny. Uncle.
-Julio's men tried to…

56
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:04,017
…run us over while we were marching.

57
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:04,851
What?

58
00:03:05,935 --> 00:03:07,562
Were you hurt?

59
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:09,564
Your uncle Pandoy and I are fine,

60
00:03:09,647 --> 00:03:11,441
but there were some people who got hurt.

61
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:13,151
-Where are they?
-They're in the hospital.

62
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:14,986
But thankfully, no one died.

63
00:03:16,404 --> 00:03:17,739
We'll look for help.

64
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:19,782
-Yes.
-We'll look for help.

65
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:21,409
Don't worry.

66
00:03:21,492 --> 00:03:24,203
That old man really has no mercy.

67
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,830
-Nanny.
-He has no conscience!

68
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:27,957
That's enough. We'll look for help.

69
00:03:28,499 --> 00:03:30,585
Ana, where's Diego?

70
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:32,253
-Jepoy.
-Diego.

71
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:36,507
Divine Oytengco and Miss Cora are dead.

72
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:40,595
Only Julio would do something like that.

73
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:42,805
Now, Emilia's case
is going to be dismissed.

74
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:43,890
What?!

75
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:46,434
Jepoy, that's impossible.

76
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:48,603
They're under the
witness protection program.

77
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:50,396
There are people guarding them.

78
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,190
Yes, Ms. Camia, that's what we know.

79
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,108
But they're dead.

80
00:03:56,402 --> 00:03:57,320
[Camia gasps]

81
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:00,865
[somber music intensifies]

82
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:17,882
Diego.

83
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:21,844
I'm speaking to you as a friend.

84
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:26,557
We can't take the Ardientes
down just by protesting.

85
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:30,645
Your signs are useless
against their bullets.

86
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:33,273
Now's the time.

87
00:04:33,856 --> 00:04:34,899
We have to fight them.

88
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:36,776
We have to arm ourselves.

89
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,111
We have to fight back!

90
00:04:39,862 --> 00:04:42,865
No. Violence isn't the answer to evil.

91
00:04:43,157 --> 00:04:45,159
[tense music playing]

92
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,745
Do you even hear yourself?

93
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:49,831
They'll kill you all
if you don't fight back.

94
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:52,208
-You have to fight back!
-We are fighting back.

95
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,294
We're fighting back in the right way!

96
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:56,129
Tell me, what is the right thing to do?!

97
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:59,465
What good thing
has ever happened in Ardiente?!

98
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:01,009
Come on! Tell me!

99
00:05:01,301 --> 00:05:03,011
Our witnesses are dead.

100
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:05,263
People are getting hurt, Diego!

101
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:07,640
-What's the right thing to do?!
-Jepoy!

102
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:10,268
That's enough.

103
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:15,148
We use guns to protect ourselves…

104
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:16,566
-…not to kill people!
-Unbelievable!

105
00:05:16,649 --> 00:05:17,817
[Anna] Jepoy!

106
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,485
You think you're an angel.

107
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:22,280
But this town isn't a
place for angels, Diego!

108
00:05:22,363 --> 00:05:23,614
Wake up!

109
00:05:23,698 --> 00:05:24,782
-Fine.
-We have to fight back.

110
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,326
-Fine, be a killer.
-Now's the time!

111
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:28,578
Fine, go and kill them.
Let's all kill them!

112
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:30,455
How does that make us
any different from them?!

113
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:43,551
[tense music intensifies]

114
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:47,346
You're right, Diego.

115
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:50,600
Only another demon can finish them off.

116
00:05:58,149 --> 00:05:59,150
-Jepoy.
-Jepoy.

117
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:00,902
Jepoy.

118
00:06:01,527 --> 00:06:03,571
Jepoy, come on. You can't leave.

119
00:06:06,908 --> 00:06:08,993
This isn't the right place for me anymore.

120
00:06:11,871 --> 00:06:13,664
I don't know where to stand, Anna.

121
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:15,374
And where will you go?

122
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:16,834
Will you go to the Ardientes?

123
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:19,170
You're going to kill them all?

124
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:20,630
That's exactly what I'll do.

125
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,258
This is the only way, Anna.

126
00:06:24,342 --> 00:06:26,844
I have to do this. I don't
want anyone else getting hurt.

127
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:28,179
No, Jepoy.

128
00:06:28,679 --> 00:06:31,599
If you won't stay, I'm coming with you.

129
00:06:31,682 --> 00:06:33,893
I won't let you hurt yourself.

130
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:40,483
Jepoy, do you understand me?

131
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:43,027
Don't leave, Jepoy.

132
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:45,905
Who knows what will happen to you?

133
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:48,324
[somber music playing]

134
00:06:49,367 --> 00:06:51,786
Please don't go.

135
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:56,749
Ivy and I need you.

136
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:03,422
Do you understand me?

137
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,675
Thank you for everything, Anna.

138
00:07:07,009 --> 00:07:08,427
Take care of yourself.

139
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:10,054
Take care of Ivy.

140
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,597
Always help her out.

141
00:07:11,889 --> 00:07:13,850
-[Anna crying]
-Thank you, Anna.

142
00:07:14,892 --> 00:07:17,103
Jepoy, please.

143
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:23,025
Jepoy!

144
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:26,821
Jepoy, please don't do this!

145
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:32,493
-Jepoy!
-You don't have to do this.

146
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:38,249
Don't.

147
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:55,892
[ominous music playing]

148
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:15,578
Madam, I've found her.

149
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:19,999
[ominous music intensifies]

150
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:27,548
Ma'am, ma'am.

151
00:08:30,384 --> 00:08:32,303
Somebody wants to give you this.

152
00:08:38,601 --> 00:08:39,477
Who?

153
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:40,895
Him.

154
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:52,907
[ominous music intensifies]

155
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,171
Please, don't. Don't!

156
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:09,757
Please, don't! Don't! Don't!

157
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,551
Don't [Emilia shouts]

158
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:14,929
Hurry. Get her inside.

159
00:09:27,483 --> 00:09:29,402
[sinister music playing]

160
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:32,989
Who are you?!

161
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:35,074
What is this place?!
Why did you bring me here?!

162
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:37,827
Stop right there! I'm warning you.

163
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:40,621
The last guy who tried to take
advantage of me is dead now!

164
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:42,415
We won't do that to you.

165
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,876
Then, why did you bring me here?!

166
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,837
Are you one of Papa's men?!

167
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:49,922
Did he order you to kill me?!

168
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:52,842
Then, don't waste your time
and just kill me!

169
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:54,885
We're not going to kill you.

170
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:57,013
Then why did you bring me here?!

171
00:09:58,264 --> 00:09:59,849
Who are you?!

172
00:10:00,766 --> 00:10:02,476
Take a shower and clean yourself up.

173
00:10:02,893 --> 00:10:04,145
Then, get changed.

174
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,564
Later, you'll have a visitor.

175
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:08,065
A visitor?

176
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:09,108
Let's go.

177
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,319
Wait! Who are you?!

178
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:13,237
Why did you bring me here?

179
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:14,989
Hey!

180
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:19,827
[slow tense music playing]

181
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:34,258
Atty. De Jesus?

182
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:37,803
Emilia, we've been
looking all over for you.

183
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:40,264
These guys kidnapped me.

184
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:42,350
I don't even know why I'm here.

185
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:44,685
Hold on, Attorney,
what are you doing here?

186
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:47,855
They abducted me and brought
me here to tell you the news.

187
00:10:47,938 --> 00:10:49,774
Huh? What news?

188
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,317
Haven't you heard?

189
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,152
The judge already dismissed your case.

190
00:10:54,278 --> 00:10:55,613
How did that happen?

191
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:58,449
Divine Oytengco
and Corazon Samartino are dead.

192
00:10:58,532 --> 00:11:01,243
The prosecution cannot present
any more witnesses.

193
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:03,746
All the evidence against you
also disappeared.

194
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:06,749
Even the jailbreaking charges
against you have been dropped.

195
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:08,959
My charges got dropped?

196
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:11,128
Who helped me?

197
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:14,006
I don't know, Emilia.

198
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:20,638
Who ordered you to kidnap me?

199
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:22,681
Come on! Answer me!

200
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:26,894
You won't stay here long, Mrs. Torillo.

201
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:31,232
We'll take you to Poblacion
Ardiente as soon as possible.

202
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:33,734
I can't leave this place yet.

203
00:11:34,318 --> 00:11:36,529
I still need a car and a phone.

204
00:11:42,034 --> 00:11:43,285
[Ivy] <i>What kind of nonsense is this?!</i>

205
00:11:43,369 --> 00:11:45,496
How could Emilia's case get dropped?

206
00:11:45,579 --> 00:11:47,623
I'm sorry, Ivy, but they got everything.

207
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:50,334
All of our evidence
and documents are gone!

208
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:51,752
It's as if none of it existed.

209
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:53,170
Okay, fine! I get it!

210
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:54,338
But, who did it?!

211
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:57,550
Who else could've helped Emilia?!

212
00:11:57,633 --> 00:11:59,760
It can't possibly be Julio.

213
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:03,055
He would never help Emilia
after she betrayed him.

214
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:05,891
If it's not Julio,

215
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:09,103
then Jaguar's probably behind this.

216
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:12,148
[tense music playing]

217
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:17,319
[raindrops pattering]

218
00:12:17,403 --> 00:12:18,612
Thank you.

219
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:23,075
Jaguar.

220
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:25,202
Jaguar, thank you.

221
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,413
You know, I've been trying to call you,

222
00:12:27,496 --> 00:12:29,457
but I cannot seem to contact you.

223
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,959
But finally, you're here.

224
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,170
Finally, I have the chance to talk to you.

225
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:36,922
I just want to thank you for saving me.

226
00:12:37,673 --> 00:12:39,925
We had to move our headquarters.

227
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:41,427
What happened to you?

228
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:44,889
What? You mean to say

229
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:48,893
that you haven't heard about
what happened to me?

230
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:52,104
Jaguar, you saved me.

231
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:55,357
You're the one who cleared
all the evidence against me.

232
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,818
You even got rid of the witnesses
so I could be free.

233
00:12:57,902 --> 00:13:00,237
I'm technically free
because of you, Jaguar.

234
00:13:01,238 --> 00:13:02,948
I'm not the one who helped you, Emilia.

235
00:13:04,408 --> 00:13:05,409
What?

236
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:07,870
You've got to be kidding me, right?

237
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:10,581
I wish I had, but I couldn't.

238
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:13,542
Okay.

239
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:15,753
If you weren't the one
who helped me, then who did?

240
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:17,755
It was Julio.

241
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:21,217
That's impossible, Jaguar!

242
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,093
My father already disowned me.

243
00:13:23,177 --> 00:13:24,929
He said he no longer has a daughter.

244
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:27,431
So, my father couldn't possibly
have helped me!

245
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:29,934
He probably needs something from you.

246
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:33,395
If Julio helped you, I'm sure
he expects something in return.

247
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:37,149
That's why you have to gain his trust

248
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:39,777
and make sure he doesn't outwit you.

249
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:48,452
[heart rate monitor beeping]

250
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:53,999
Governor, Mr. Chen sent these.

251
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:55,209
Oh!

252
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:59,421
Well, please tell Mr. Chen,

253
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:02,591
thank you for his gift,

254
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:05,344
and I'm looking forward to

255
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:07,555
working with him some more in the future.

256
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:09,390
-Yes, Governor.
-Please put it there.

257
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:15,062
Okay. Please let my visitor in.

258
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:16,814
-Okay, Governor.
-Okay.

259
00:14:22,194 --> 00:14:23,404
[Julio chuckles]

260
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:28,909
Oh, car keys.

261
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:32,371
[suspenseful music playing]

262
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:35,833
Money, money, money, money, money, money.

263
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:39,712
See, Arnaldo?

264
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:45,134
That is why we spend
millions during elections,

265
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:46,844
to make sure that we'll win.

266
00:14:47,636 --> 00:14:52,224
So that we can make… more… millions.

267
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,727
You see? That's the point.

268
00:14:58,188 --> 00:14:59,648
[Julio chuckles]

269
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:02,902
The reason why there should always be

270
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:05,738
an Ardiente holding a
position in the government…

271
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:09,867
is to ensure that
we continue raking in money.

272
00:15:12,369 --> 00:15:14,246
But it seems like…

273
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:17,416
we have a problem right now.

274
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:25,257
Looks like we harbored a traitor
under our roof, and…

275
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:28,928
you know who that person is.

276
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:36,352
Does the name Ivy Aguas ring a bell?

277
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,605
Arnaldo, is this woman…

278
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:44,610
an enemy or not, huh?

279
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:51,033
Well, doesn't really matter, my son.

280
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:57,081
We're about to find out
that woman's true allegiance

281
00:15:57,164 --> 00:16:00,626
and Grandpa Julio
will take care of everything.

282
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:07,132
Once I prove that she's betraying us,

283
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:13,597
I'll put a bullet in her head

284
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:18,185
and feed her to street rats.

285
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:22,815
[knocking on door]

286
00:16:22,898 --> 00:16:24,692
-[tense music playing]
-Come in. Come in.

287
00:16:25,859 --> 00:16:26,944
Governor.

288
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:32,658
Is this what they mean when they say:

289
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:36,912
"to the victor belongs the spoils"?

290
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:40,124
Something like that.

291
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:41,625
How are you, Ms. Aguas?

292
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:43,419
Yes.

293
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,964
So, why were you looking for me?

294
00:16:48,882 --> 00:16:49,925
Well…

295
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:53,971
someone told me that Diego's group

296
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:59,309
is planning to cause trouble again,

297
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:02,855
and it seems like they just
don't know when to quit!

298
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:07,818
Okay. So, what do you plan
to do with them?

299
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:12,781
What does a father do
to his rebellious children?

300
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:15,409
Shouldn't he teach them a lesson?

301
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,912
This might be against my will,

302
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:21,290
but I need to do this.

303
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:25,878
And I choose you, Ms. Aguas,

304
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:30,883
to carry out their punishment.

305
00:17:32,342 --> 00:17:33,469
[tense music playing]

306
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:36,930
So, go with the Colonel.

307
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:39,475
Take them. Capture them.

308
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:40,851
Talk to them.

309
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:44,980
Kidnap whoever you see in Diego's camp.

310
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,231
After that…

311
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,819
turn them into ash, okay?

312
00:17:50,903 --> 00:17:53,655
Me?! Why me?

313
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:55,783
What use is the Colonel then?

314
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:56,992
Is he useless now?

315
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,410
What about your other men?

316
00:17:58,494 --> 00:17:59,912
You want me to do it?

317
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:02,414
You know, Miss Aguas,

318
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:05,501
I chose you because I noticed that

319
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:08,545
when it comes to Diego's group…

320
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:12,758
you become weak.

321
00:18:15,886 --> 00:18:18,889
I think I need to toughen you up.

322
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:23,352
I need to make sure you can still help me,

323
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:24,812
and that you're on my side.

324
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:27,898
Governor, what else do you want from me?

325
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:29,024
Tell me!

326
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:31,819
I risked my life for Arnaldo.

327
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:34,780
I provided a huge amount
of money to fund your campaign.

328
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:37,783
And yet, you're still suspicious of me.

329
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:40,869
What else can I do to prove my loyalty?

330
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:43,747
Well, that's easy.

331
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:47,292
Just do what I asked you to do.

332
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:50,420
Kill Diego's men.

333
00:18:52,756 --> 00:18:53,841
[Ivy] No.

334
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:57,261
Well, you choose.

335
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:58,595
Either you kill them…

336
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:11,150
…or I kill you.

337
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,946
[tense music intensifies]

338
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:27,249
Four against one?

339
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:33,463
The odds aren't in your favor, Ms. Aguas.

340
00:19:39,094 --> 00:19:41,930
I'm giving you a choice, Ms. Aguas.

341
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:44,808
Kill…

342
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:49,688
…or be killed.

343
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:52,774
Let go of your gun.

344
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:04,244
If you weren't a soulless,
cold-hearted person like me,

345
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:09,708
you wouldn't survive in my world.

346
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:12,878
Is that what you want me to do?

347
00:20:13,378 --> 00:20:15,923
Eliminate all of Diego's men?

348
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:17,174
Something like that.

349
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:18,884
I want to see…

350
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:21,720
their blood on your hands.

351
00:20:23,055 --> 00:20:24,056
Okay.

352
00:20:24,681 --> 00:20:25,432
Fine.

353
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,476
If it will make you happy,

354
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:28,810
I'll do it.

355
00:20:31,396 --> 00:20:33,774
But I want something in return.

356
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:36,944
Oh, tit for tat. Name it.

357
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:41,490
I want to be involved in all
of your business transactions,

358
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:43,325
legal or illegal.

359
00:20:43,408 --> 00:20:47,704
I want a bigger piece of the pie.

360
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:49,957
[Julio chuckles]

361
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:53,210
Money and greed.

362
00:20:53,293 --> 00:20:54,878
At the end of the day,

363
00:20:55,462 --> 00:20:57,798
it still boils down to that.

364
00:21:00,133 --> 00:21:01,260
Agreed.

365
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:12,646
[suspenseful music playing]

366
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:23,573
This is just the beginning
of Julio's vicious plans.

367
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:27,536
Many more will be affected and get hurt.

368
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:30,706
That's why I won't blame you if…

369
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:33,709
you want to back down.

370
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:38,297
I don't want any of you to get hurt,

371
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:41,258
so I'm letting you
return to your families.

372
00:21:41,883 --> 00:21:43,260
Live a peaceful life,

373
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:47,389
a life free from fear.

374
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:52,185
But I promise that I'll continue
this fight, no matter what.

375
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:54,479
I won't give up.

376
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:56,648
That's a promise.

377
00:21:57,607 --> 00:22:00,027
So, please go home. You too, Marlon.

378
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:02,279
We're not leaving you, Diego.

379
00:22:02,362 --> 00:22:03,989
We're not afraid of Julio.

380
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:05,991
We'll fight with you until the end.

381
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:09,328
As long as you're with us,
we won't lose hope.

382
00:22:09,411 --> 00:22:11,872
We'll fight for a new Ardiente!

383
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:13,415
[uplifting music playing]

384
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:14,458
Yes!

385
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:15,667
-We'll fight.
-We'll fight on.

386
00:22:16,251 --> 00:22:17,336
We will fight.

387
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:18,837
-Right.
-We will fight.

388
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:19,838
Fight!

389
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:22,007
Fight on, son!

390
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:23,842
We'll fight on.

391
00:22:24,384 --> 00:22:25,427
Fight!

392
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:27,888
-Fight.
-We will fight!

393
00:22:27,971 --> 00:22:29,222
Fight!

394
00:22:30,766 --> 00:22:32,267
Thank you, everyone.

395
00:22:47,866 --> 00:22:51,411
[line ringing]

396
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:54,831
Oh, Ivy.

397
00:22:56,291 --> 00:22:57,334
You are still here.

398
00:22:57,417 --> 00:22:58,585
Are you surprised?

399
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:01,838
I'm no longer a corrupt queen.

400
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:03,590
I am the real queen,

401
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:05,425
and I am so back!

402
00:23:06,718 --> 00:23:08,553
Well, welcome back, corruption queen!

403
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:10,097
You should've told me you were coming.

404
00:23:10,180 --> 00:23:11,598
I would've hired a caterer…

405
00:23:11,681 --> 00:23:13,141
-No need.
-…and a band.

406
00:23:14,142 --> 00:23:17,479
Actually, I came here
to surprise everyone.

407
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:21,108
You're lucky I didn't catch you scheming.

408
00:23:21,191 --> 00:23:22,818
Oh, come on, Emilia.

409
00:23:22,901 --> 00:23:24,361
Me, scheming?

410
00:23:24,444 --> 00:23:27,322
You've never caught me
because I'm innocent.

411
00:23:27,405 --> 00:23:30,408
Let's be honest, in this household,

412
00:23:30,492 --> 00:23:33,787
you're the one who's always
scheming behind people's backs.

413
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:36,206
So you told Papa on me?!

414
00:23:36,289 --> 00:23:38,458
Don't you ever accuse me of something

415
00:23:38,542 --> 00:23:40,877
you can't even prove.

416
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:44,089
Go on, Ivy! Keep lying!

417
00:23:44,172 --> 00:23:45,882
I'm not stupid, you know.

418
00:23:46,424 --> 00:23:48,844
But, let me just remind you, Ivy,

419
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:51,847
that I am so back here in this house.

420
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:54,224
This is my family, and this is my house,

421
00:23:54,307 --> 00:23:57,060
and whether you like it or not,
I am going to stay here!

422
00:23:57,686 --> 00:23:58,687
[Emilia chuckles]

423
00:23:58,770 --> 00:23:59,855
Emilia.

424
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:01,648
Hi, Papa.

425
00:24:02,774 --> 00:24:04,776
[tense music playing]

426
00:24:28,425 --> 00:24:32,053
[tense music playing]

427
00:24:43,982 --> 00:24:45,942
Boss Jaguar couldn't have gotten far.

428
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:47,903
He was shot.

429
00:24:48,403 --> 00:24:49,821
He could be hiding around here.

430
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:51,156
What if he's dead?

431
00:24:52,407 --> 00:24:53,783
We have to make sure.

432
00:25:08,256 --> 00:25:09,424
Damian.

433
00:25:11,885 --> 00:25:12,886
[henchman] Dude.

434
00:25:13,887 --> 00:25:14,888
Did you guys hear that?

435
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:21,019
Someone said the boss' name.

436
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:26,399
[doorbell rings]

437
00:25:27,734 --> 00:25:29,152
[knocking on gate]

438
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:30,278
Hello?

439
00:25:32,405 --> 00:25:34,824
-[knocking on gate]
-Anyone home?

440
00:25:35,825 --> 00:25:36,952
Hello.

441
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:40,997
-[knocking on gate]
-Anyone home?

442
00:25:42,999 --> 00:25:44,000
What's going on?

443
00:25:44,876 --> 00:25:46,795
Dude, I don't think he's in there.

444
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:48,004
But I heard someone say "Damian".

445
00:25:48,088 --> 00:25:49,714
Is he the only person named Damian?

446
00:25:51,174 --> 00:25:52,259
Come on.

447
00:25:57,305 --> 00:25:58,556
Papa.

448
00:25:58,932 --> 00:26:01,893
I came here because
I want to know the truth.

449
00:26:04,729 --> 00:26:06,690
Are you the one who cleared my case?

450
00:26:18,201 --> 00:26:19,327
What do you think?

451
00:26:23,873 --> 00:26:28,211
Who do you think would help you?

452
00:26:30,422 --> 00:26:31,548
You know, Emilia,

453
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:36,928
I wanted to make sure
I'd win in the election.

454
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:39,931
When I knew that,

455
00:26:41,057 --> 00:26:43,435
I went to clear your case right away.

456
00:26:45,395 --> 00:26:46,855
Thank you, Papa.

457
00:26:48,606 --> 00:26:50,942
Does that mean you've forgiven me?

458
00:26:53,403 --> 00:26:55,864
No matter what you did against me,

459
00:26:58,199 --> 00:27:00,452
you're still my daughter, Emilia.

460
00:27:03,246 --> 00:27:04,622
And as your father,

461
00:27:05,915 --> 00:27:10,879
I am obligated to take care of you.

462
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:13,923
Emilia.

463
00:27:14,841 --> 00:27:17,635
You are an Ardiente.

464
00:27:18,887 --> 00:27:20,889
And that is one thing…

465
00:27:22,390 --> 00:27:24,225
that will never change,

466
00:27:25,643 --> 00:27:28,396
whether I like it or not.

467
00:27:28,855 --> 00:27:30,440
Papa, thank you.

468
00:27:33,401 --> 00:27:34,402
Thank you, Papa.

469
00:27:39,366 --> 00:27:40,200
Thank you.

470
00:27:40,867 --> 00:27:42,744
Papa, I promise you,

471
00:27:43,286 --> 00:27:45,830
you're not going to regret
giving me a second chance.

472
00:27:45,914 --> 00:27:47,582
I'm going to prove to you my worth.

473
00:27:47,665 --> 00:27:48,958
I'm not going to betray you again.

474
00:27:49,042 --> 00:27:50,835
I will cut my ties with Jaguar.

475
00:27:50,919 --> 00:27:52,670
I promise you that, Papa.

476
00:27:52,754 --> 00:27:54,172
I promise.

477
00:28:04,974 --> 00:28:06,267
[Ivy] <i>Go figure.</i>

478
00:28:06,893 --> 00:28:09,813
<i>Like father, like daughter.</i>

479
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:14,150
<i>Those two are cut</i>
<i>from the same two-faced cloth.</i>

480
00:28:17,612 --> 00:28:19,364
[mouthing] Bravo.

481
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:23,952
Who were those men, Damian?

482
00:28:24,327 --> 00:28:25,662
Why are you hiding from them?

483
00:28:29,666 --> 00:28:31,418
Tell me the truth.

484
00:28:33,711 --> 00:28:36,798
If I find out you still haven't
given up being a criminal,

485
00:28:37,424 --> 00:28:39,342
I will personally bring you to jail,

486
00:28:39,426 --> 00:28:40,677
just like what your brother did.

487
00:28:43,596 --> 00:28:44,931
I'm not a criminal, Camia.

488
00:28:45,014 --> 00:28:48,476
Those were the men who robbed me.

489
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:50,562
Why didn't you go to the police?

490
00:28:50,854 --> 00:28:52,147
I don't want trouble.

491
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:53,565
You might get involved.

492
00:28:53,648 --> 00:28:55,900
I just want a quiet life.

493
00:28:55,984 --> 00:28:57,610
You don't want trouble, Damian?

494
00:28:58,403 --> 00:29:00,405
Or are you hiding something from me?

495
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:03,825
Camia, believe me. I've changed.

496
00:29:04,409 --> 00:29:06,870
I'm not a criminal anymore.

497
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:10,874
I live a completely different life now.

498
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:12,876
I have to admit,

499
00:29:14,377 --> 00:29:16,755
I still don't completely
trust you, Damian.

500
00:29:18,131 --> 00:29:21,885
But I'll give you a chance
to prove yourself.

501
00:29:22,802 --> 00:29:25,430
But the moment I find out
that you're lying to us,

502
00:29:25,889 --> 00:29:27,932
I will never forgive you.

503
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:35,482
[tense music playing]

504
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:48,369
-[oxygen machine running]
-[heart rate monitor beeping]

505
00:29:58,880 --> 00:30:00,006
[Emilia crying]

506
00:30:00,423 --> 00:30:01,883
How are you, my son?

507
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:04,177
Mommy's back.

508
00:30:06,679 --> 00:30:07,514
[exhales sharply]

509
00:30:09,766 --> 00:30:10,892
I missed you.

510
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:17,232
-[machine beeps]
-Arnaldo.

511
00:30:18,858 --> 00:30:20,401
Do you think…

512
00:30:21,569 --> 00:30:25,907
your grandfather really
helped me with my case?

513
00:30:30,078 --> 00:30:33,373
If it wasn't your grandfather or Jaguar,

514
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:38,419
who else would want to be
involved in my life?

515
00:30:39,128 --> 00:30:40,880
[cell phone ringing]

516
00:30:42,423 --> 00:30:43,675
Hello, Attorney.

517
00:30:44,467 --> 00:30:47,178
Have you done what I asked you to do?

518
00:30:47,428 --> 00:30:48,513
Yes, Emilia.

519
00:30:48,596 --> 00:30:51,516
I tracked down the owner of the
house those men brought you to.

520
00:30:51,599 --> 00:30:53,643
<i>I also did some research</i>
<i>on that car they let you use.</i>

521
00:30:53,726 --> 00:30:56,479
They're both registered
to one Mercedes Palacio.

522
00:30:56,896 --> 00:30:58,690
Huh? Who is that?

523
00:30:58,773 --> 00:31:00,108
It's an alias.

524
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:02,610
<i>No one knows who this person is.</i>

525
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:04,946
We're not even sure
if she's actually she or a he.

526
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:07,699
Plenty of men use female names
as their aliases

527
00:31:07,782 --> 00:31:10,326
<i>to confuse anybody probing</i>
<i>for their real identity.</i>

528
00:31:10,660 --> 00:31:13,329
So, Attorney, there is still a possibility

529
00:31:13,413 --> 00:31:15,748
that my father helped me?

530
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:19,002
At this point,
anything is possible, Emilia.

531
00:31:26,050 --> 00:31:27,343
[Julio] Sanggano.

532
00:31:28,094 --> 00:31:31,723
I want you to have our people figure out

533
00:31:32,432 --> 00:31:36,144
who fixed Emilia's case.

534
00:31:36,853 --> 00:31:39,272
Governor, didn't you help Emilia?

535
00:31:40,857 --> 00:31:43,401
I've already disowned
that daughter of mine.

536
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:47,906
I can't forgive her
for what she did to me.

537
00:31:49,115 --> 00:31:52,827
I just let her believe
that I was responsible

538
00:31:52,911 --> 00:31:54,871
for fixing her case.

539
00:31:55,496 --> 00:31:56,831
But the truth is,

540
00:31:57,373 --> 00:32:00,919
I just want to know who really did.

541
00:32:02,086 --> 00:32:03,796
Because one day,

542
00:32:03,880 --> 00:32:06,341
that person might be a threat to us.

543
00:32:06,883 --> 00:32:08,927
Conduct a thorough investigation,

544
00:32:09,636 --> 00:32:13,973
but make sure Emilia doesn't
find out what you're doing.

545
00:32:14,849 --> 00:32:17,393
Jaguar's the only other person
who could help Emilia, right?

546
00:32:17,477 --> 00:32:18,269
[chuckles]

547
00:32:19,854 --> 00:32:23,316
Don't be so sure, Sanggano.

548
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:27,987
There's a lot you don't know about Emilia.

549
00:32:29,405 --> 00:32:30,490
Yes, Governor.

550
00:32:35,286 --> 00:32:37,288
[ominous music playing]

551
00:32:50,426 --> 00:32:53,888
The two of you will investigate
Ma'am Emilia's acquittal.

552
00:32:54,639 --> 00:32:56,349
I expect a report by tonight.

553
00:32:56,432 --> 00:32:57,433
-Yes, sir.
-Go on.

554
00:33:00,395 --> 00:33:01,646
You two, come with me.

555
00:33:02,063 --> 00:33:03,231
We have another assignment.

556
00:33:03,314 --> 00:33:04,440
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

557
00:33:08,778 --> 00:33:10,571
Ms. Ivy Aguas.

558
00:33:11,489 --> 00:33:12,824
Where are you going?

559
00:33:13,408 --> 00:33:16,411
-It's none of your business.
-Wait. You can't leave.

560
00:33:16,869 --> 00:33:18,204
Governor's orders.

561
00:33:18,871 --> 00:33:21,332
We're attacking Diego's group tonight.

562
00:33:25,420 --> 00:33:27,296
[suspenseful music playing]

563
00:33:40,643 --> 00:33:43,855
[Emilia] <i>You're hiding</i>
<i>too many secrets, Papa.</i>

564
00:33:44,397 --> 00:33:46,399
<i>I need to get close to you.</i>

565
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:47,984
<i>Really close.</i>

566
00:33:48,067 --> 00:33:51,404
<i>To dig into your deepest</i>
<i>and darkest secrets.</i>

567
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:56,409
<i>And I have to get rid of your</i>
<i>favorite pet, Ivy, to get there.</i>

568
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:06,377
What the hell are you doing here?

569
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:08,004
Hi, Papa.

570
00:34:11,424 --> 00:34:13,718
I came here to…

571
00:34:14,427 --> 00:34:17,180
make up for all my mistakes.

572
00:34:18,431 --> 00:34:22,602
I was going to suggest something
if you're up to it.

573
00:34:29,942 --> 00:34:30,735
-Hey.
-I'll do it.

574
00:34:30,818 --> 00:34:32,195
Lift it up.

575
00:34:33,154 --> 00:34:33,988
Okay.

576
00:34:34,530 --> 00:34:35,573
-Take care.
-Yeah.

577
00:34:35,656 --> 00:34:37,784
-Thanks.
-Take care, all of you.

578
00:34:37,867 --> 00:34:40,620
-Bye.
-We have a long day tomorrow.

579
00:34:40,703 --> 00:34:43,873
[Loring] Okay. Take care. Yeah. Oh, okay.

580
00:34:44,499 --> 00:34:46,084
Let's talk tomorrow.

581
00:34:46,167 --> 00:34:47,210
Oh! What's this?

582
00:34:47,293 --> 00:34:49,170
-Hey, what's happening?!
-[tires screeching]

583
00:34:49,253 --> 00:34:50,713
-Auntie! Auntie!
-What's happening?

584
00:34:50,797 --> 00:34:53,132
-[gunshots]
-[woman screams]

585
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:56,761
[screaming]

586
00:34:57,553 --> 00:34:58,679
What's this?

587
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:00,598
Where are you taking us?! Huh?!

588
00:35:00,681 --> 00:35:02,100
Auntie Camia, stay here, okay?

589
00:35:02,183 --> 00:35:03,184
Batch, look after her.

590
00:35:03,267 --> 00:35:04,268
-Okay.
-Diego.

591
00:35:04,852 --> 00:35:07,313
-Wait a minute!
-Auntie! Wait!

592
00:35:07,396 --> 00:35:08,981
-Hurry up!
-Don't hurt us!

593
00:35:09,357 --> 00:35:11,109
Auntie Camia, I'm going to help Diego.

594
00:35:12,819 --> 00:35:14,570
[Loring] Wait! Pandoy!

595
00:35:14,654 --> 00:35:17,281
Pandoy! Pandoy! Wait a minute!

596
00:35:17,365 --> 00:35:19,033
-[gunshots]
-[Loring shouts]

597
00:35:20,660 --> 00:35:21,577
Diego!

598
00:35:22,870 --> 00:35:24,038
Diego!

599
00:35:24,122 --> 00:35:25,998
-Diego!
-[engine starts]

600
00:35:26,415 --> 00:35:29,168
-Diego, help us!
-Anna, don't worry!

601
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:31,712
-[gunshots]
-[tires screeching]

602
00:35:32,839 --> 00:35:34,423
Wait! Hey!

603
00:35:38,845 --> 00:35:40,888
Auntie, those were our people.

604
00:35:41,222 --> 00:35:42,640
Diego, I'm going to get help.

605
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:45,518
Diego, call my daughter.

606
00:35:47,854 --> 00:35:50,148
She might know something!
This might be Julio's doing!

607
00:35:53,860 --> 00:35:55,111
[line ringing]

608
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:56,863
[phone vibrates]

609
00:36:03,369 --> 00:36:04,871
[line ringing]

610
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:06,706
[phone vibrates]

611
00:36:06,789 --> 00:36:08,416
Aren't you going to answer that?

612
00:36:11,586 --> 00:36:12,628
She's not picking up.

613
00:36:12,712 --> 00:36:14,297
Come on. Let's go inside.

614
00:36:17,300 --> 00:36:18,426
No.

615
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:20,303
What's it to you?

616
00:36:21,429 --> 00:36:23,890
I don't have to answer
an unimportant call.

617
00:36:26,893 --> 00:36:27,935
Let's go.

618
00:36:31,397 --> 00:36:32,857
[car engine starts]

619
00:36:39,488 --> 00:36:42,325
The judge who dismissed
Mrs. Emilia's case is missing.

620
00:36:42,408 --> 00:36:44,327
And no one knows if he was paid to do it,

621
00:36:44,410 --> 00:36:45,828
or who paid him.

622
00:36:45,912 --> 00:36:48,873
We also can't find the one
who took all the evidence.

623
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:50,583
I'm sorry, Governor.

624
00:36:50,666 --> 00:36:51,834
We did everything we could

625
00:36:51,918 --> 00:36:53,920
to find whoever helped Ma'am Emilia.

626
00:36:54,420 --> 00:36:56,339
But everyone we asked

627
00:36:56,422 --> 00:36:57,965
seemed scared to talk about her.

628
00:36:58,883 --> 00:37:00,843
Whoever it is,

629
00:37:02,929 --> 00:37:06,432
they can't hide from me forever.

630
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:11,437
Call Colonel Sanggano.

631
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:15,650
I need to talk to him
about Ivy Aguas' mission.

632
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:17,401
Yes, Governor.

633
00:37:19,820 --> 00:37:21,822
[tense music playing]

634
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:24,951
Go inside!

635
00:37:25,034 --> 00:37:27,328
-What's happening?
-Auntie Loring!

636
00:37:27,411 --> 00:37:29,830
-Please spare us!
-Hurry!

637
00:37:29,914 --> 00:37:31,832
-What gives?!
-Move!

638
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:34,335
-Have mercy!
-Please, have mercy!

639
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:35,753
What will you do to us?

640
00:37:37,004 --> 00:37:38,339
All of you!

641
00:37:38,923 --> 00:37:40,633
-Shut up!
-Be quiet.

642
00:37:40,716 --> 00:37:42,343
Especially you two.

643
00:37:42,426 --> 00:37:44,178
Okay, tie them all up.

644
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:46,347
-[cell phone ringing]
-Please, have mercy.

645
00:37:46,430 --> 00:37:47,390
Hurry!

646
00:37:47,473 --> 00:37:50,559
-Help!
-Have mercy, sir.

647
00:37:50,643 --> 00:37:51,644
[Jose] Yes, Governor?

648
00:37:52,103 --> 00:37:53,145
Okay, Governor.

649
00:37:54,855 --> 00:37:56,607
Wait for the others. They're on their way.

650
00:37:56,691 --> 00:37:58,859
Make sure no one escapes.

651
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:00,444
Yes, Boss.

652
00:38:04,115 --> 00:38:06,200
The governor wants me to take you home.

653
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:09,328
Why? What are we going to do
with the hostages?

654
00:38:09,412 --> 00:38:11,789
Are we leaving them here?
What are you planning to do?

655
00:38:11,872 --> 00:38:13,791
Just follow me.
The governor changed his plan.

656
00:38:13,874 --> 00:38:15,668
Then, tell me what the new plan is.

657
00:38:15,751 --> 00:38:18,087
[sighs] It doesn't involve you,
Ms. Aguas. Let's go.

658
00:38:18,170 --> 00:38:20,006
-Colonel, hey!
-Let's go.

659
00:38:21,632 --> 00:38:23,843
-[clamoring]
-What did we do to you?

660
00:38:23,926 --> 00:38:26,721
-Silence!
-Shut up!

661
00:38:26,804 --> 00:38:29,807
-We didn't do anything.
-Shut up!

662
00:38:29,890 --> 00:38:32,685
-Hey!
-Why are you doing this to us?!

663
00:38:32,768 --> 00:38:34,812
-We didn't do anything wrong!
-Please let us go!

664
00:38:34,895 --> 00:38:37,315
We didn't do anything wrong!

665
00:38:38,190 --> 00:38:41,777
-Hey! Come back here!
-Somebody, help us!

666
00:38:41,861 --> 00:38:43,696
Stop moving around! Someone, help us!

667
00:38:45,072 --> 00:38:46,907
Governor, you have a visitor.

668
00:38:46,991 --> 00:38:48,326
It's Diego Torillo.

669
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:50,244
Let him in.

670
00:38:52,997 --> 00:38:53,914
Oh…

671
00:38:54,832 --> 00:38:56,000
Diego.

672
00:38:56,417 --> 00:38:58,961
What are you doing here?

673
00:38:59,754 --> 00:39:04,300
Didn't we teach you decency and
courtesy when you were younger?

674
00:39:04,884 --> 00:39:06,802
Where did you take my supporters?

675
00:39:07,261 --> 00:39:08,596
What did you do to them?

676
00:39:09,388 --> 00:39:10,973
Who's "them"?

677
00:39:11,432 --> 00:39:14,643
I don't know who the hell
you're talking about.

678
00:39:14,727 --> 00:39:17,396
Stop acting innocent, Governor.

679
00:39:18,522 --> 00:39:20,316
I'm the one you want to hurt, right?

680
00:39:20,399 --> 00:39:22,985
So, take me and release my supporters.

681
00:39:23,402 --> 00:39:27,114
Why do you always blame me

682
00:39:27,198 --> 00:39:29,867
whenever something bad
happens to your supporters?

683
00:39:30,868 --> 00:39:35,873
Why don't you ask
Ms. Ivy Aguas for a change?

684
00:39:37,249 --> 00:39:38,834
Because from what I heard,

685
00:39:38,918 --> 00:39:41,796
she was the one who
had your people abducted.

686
00:39:43,422 --> 00:39:44,423
What?

687
00:39:45,091 --> 00:39:46,092
Surprised?

688
00:39:47,426 --> 00:39:48,636
Why don't you call her?

689
00:39:48,719 --> 00:39:50,846
I know you have her number.

690
00:39:52,890 --> 00:39:55,559
Have you two been talking
more often recently?

691
00:39:57,019 --> 00:39:59,230
I don't have time to joke around with you.

692
00:39:59,855 --> 00:40:01,190
And whatever your plan is,

693
00:40:01,982 --> 00:40:04,402
I'll make sure you won't succeed.

694
00:40:12,660 --> 00:40:14,537
Make sure…

695
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:19,375
Diego won't get in the way of my plans.

696
00:40:19,458 --> 00:40:20,418
Yes, sir.

697
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:30,678
You can't leave until
the Governor says so.

698
00:40:30,970 --> 00:40:31,971
Understand?

699
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:36,851
Tell the Governor he can't
just order me around.

700
00:40:36,934 --> 00:40:38,602
I'm not afraid of him.

701
00:40:39,103 --> 00:40:42,398
Don't disobey him
if you don't want any trouble.

702
00:40:49,864 --> 00:40:51,407
[engine starts]

703
00:41:07,339 --> 00:41:08,883
[phone ringing]

704
00:41:10,050 --> 00:41:10,801
Hello.

705
00:41:11,886 --> 00:41:12,887
[Julio] <i>All right.</i>

706
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:14,597
Follow her.

707
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:16,807
[engine starts]

708
00:41:26,984 --> 00:41:28,861
[suspenseful music playing]

709
00:41:29,695 --> 00:41:30,738
Auntie.

710
00:41:30,821 --> 00:41:32,907
Diego, what did Julio say?

711
00:41:32,990 --> 00:41:34,825
He said that Ivy's behind the kidnapping.

712
00:41:34,909 --> 00:41:36,827
-Huh?
-I've been trying to call her…

713
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:37,912
…but I can't reach her.

714
00:41:40,206 --> 00:41:41,832
<i>The subscriber cannot be reached.</i>

715
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:43,751
Auntie, I have a bad feeling about this.

716
00:41:43,834 --> 00:41:45,836
Julio seems to know something about Ivy.

717
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:47,171
My goodness.

718
00:41:50,007 --> 00:41:52,343
-Hey!
-Help us!

719
00:41:52,426 --> 00:41:55,054
-Help us!
-Have mercy on us!

720
00:41:55,888 --> 00:41:57,890
[tense music playing]

721
00:42:05,397 --> 00:42:07,525
You, take that side. You, go there.

722
00:42:22,790 --> 00:42:23,999
[phone ringing]

723
00:42:24,500 --> 00:42:25,543
It's Ivy.

724
00:42:26,043 --> 00:42:27,711
-Hello, Ivy?
-[Ivy] <i>Diego.</i>

725
00:42:27,795 --> 00:42:31,549
Diego, Julio's men abducted
Anna and your supporters.

726
00:42:31,632 --> 00:42:32,883
They're going to kill them!

727
00:42:32,967 --> 00:42:34,093
Where did they take them?

728
00:42:34,176 --> 00:42:35,386
To San Narciso.

729
00:42:35,886 --> 00:42:37,638
Get there as soon as you can!
I'm on my way!

730
00:42:47,606 --> 00:42:49,024
-Light it up?
-Go.

731
00:42:49,108 --> 00:42:51,235
-Go, go. Set it on fire.
-Quickly. Come on!

732
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:04,582
-Hey!
-Help!

733
00:43:04,665 --> 00:43:06,875
-Hey!
-Help us!

734
00:43:11,880 --> 00:43:14,466
-Help!
-Wait!

735
00:43:14,550 --> 00:43:15,843
Help us!

736
00:43:15,926 --> 00:43:17,344
Help!

737
00:43:17,428 --> 00:43:20,806
-You bastards!
-Help! Help! Help us!

738
00:43:20,889 --> 00:43:22,891
-Someone help!
-Help us!

739
00:43:23,642 --> 00:43:25,769
Help! Help!

740
00:43:26,312 --> 00:43:28,230
Please help us!

741
00:43:30,941 --> 00:43:32,818
[crying]

742
00:43:37,948 --> 00:43:41,410
[all] Help us! Please, help us!

743
00:43:44,413 --> 00:43:46,415
[all coughing]

744
00:43:49,877 --> 00:43:51,837
[Loring shouts]

745
00:43:51,920 --> 00:43:53,339
Loring, stay strong.

746
00:43:53,422 --> 00:43:54,548
Help!

747
00:43:56,592 --> 00:43:58,927
-[people coughing]
-Help!

748
00:44:08,270 --> 00:44:10,939
Cheers, Dante.

749
00:44:16,862 --> 00:44:17,988
You're unbelievable.

750
00:44:19,073 --> 00:44:22,409
You actually went back
to try and get me out.

751
00:44:25,871 --> 00:44:27,414
You know…

752
00:44:28,874 --> 00:44:30,834
you've always been the better man.

753
00:44:31,418 --> 00:44:35,422
You were always the good guy,
the smart one.

754
00:44:36,882 --> 00:44:40,594
You even won the heart
of the woman we both love!

755
00:44:41,178 --> 00:44:42,638
It was always you!

756
00:44:43,681 --> 00:44:45,015
You had everything.

757
00:44:45,808 --> 00:44:47,393
I give up, Dante.

758
00:44:48,852 --> 00:44:50,771
You're the winner.

759
00:44:51,271 --> 00:44:53,273
[melancholic music playing]

760
00:44:54,942 --> 00:44:56,235
I give up!

761
00:44:58,862 --> 00:45:01,365
I'm tired of living like this!

762
00:45:04,743 --> 00:45:06,412
Whether or not you believe me,

763
00:45:07,413 --> 00:45:11,458
I longed to live a life like yours!

764
00:45:14,253 --> 00:45:17,965
But no one would give me the opportunity!

765
00:45:18,882 --> 00:45:20,384
No one but Camia.

766
00:45:21,427 --> 00:45:25,013
She alone gave me the chance
to turn over a new leaf!

767
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:39,903
[tense music playing]

768
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:45,909
-Help!
-Somebody help us!

769
00:46:01,884 --> 00:46:03,218
[Loring coughs]

770
00:46:04,428 --> 00:46:06,805
-Someone, help us!
-Ivy?!

771
00:46:06,889 --> 00:46:07,973
Wait!

772
00:46:08,056 --> 00:46:10,017
Ivy, we're trapped inside!

773
00:46:10,100 --> 00:46:11,393
Please help us!

774
00:46:17,816 --> 00:46:19,401
-Ivy!
-Please help us!

775
00:46:21,361 --> 00:46:22,988
[loud clattering]

776
00:46:23,864 --> 00:46:25,032
Help!

777
00:46:29,828 --> 00:46:32,831
[clattering]

778
00:46:41,882 --> 00:46:42,883
Ivy!

779
00:46:43,425 --> 00:46:45,219
-Ivy! Save us.
-Pandoy!

780
00:46:46,845 --> 00:46:48,847
[tense music playing]

781
00:46:53,852 --> 00:46:56,897
-[Loring groans]
-[Anna coughs]

782
00:46:57,856 --> 00:47:00,067
-Come on!
-Go ahead.

783
00:47:00,859 --> 00:47:02,528
-Get out of here!
-Thank you!

784
00:47:12,371 --> 00:47:13,413
[Loring coughs]

785
00:47:18,377 --> 00:47:19,419
[Anna coughs]

786
00:47:21,880 --> 00:47:23,882
[people coughing]

787
00:47:24,883 --> 00:47:26,927
You guys go ahead! Come on.

788
00:47:29,888 --> 00:47:31,265
Let's get out of here.

789
00:47:34,309 --> 00:47:35,978
[indistinct chatter, coughing]

790
00:47:36,061 --> 00:47:37,145
Let's go.

791
00:47:37,896 --> 00:47:39,398
[people continue coughing]

792
00:47:41,858 --> 00:47:42,859
Go on.

793
00:47:44,695 --> 00:47:45,612
Hey.

794
00:47:45,696 --> 00:47:47,322
Go on! Get out of here!
Get in the jeepney!

795
00:47:47,406 --> 00:47:49,783
-Ivy! Wait, what about you?
-I can take care of myself.

796
00:47:49,866 --> 00:47:51,868
Go now before Julio's men see you.

797
00:47:51,952 --> 00:47:53,745
The Ardientes might catch you.

798
00:47:53,829 --> 00:47:55,330
No, they won't. Go!

799
00:47:55,414 --> 00:47:57,708
Get on that jeepney and call Diego.

800
00:47:58,333 --> 00:48:00,586
-[jeepney engine starts]
-Take care.

801
00:48:01,169 --> 00:48:02,212
Get out of here.

802
00:48:11,722 --> 00:48:12,889
Ivy.

803
00:48:15,017 --> 00:48:16,268
Ivy.

804
00:48:17,853 --> 00:48:19,771
[Emilia laughs]

805
00:48:19,855 --> 00:48:20,897
Ivy.

806
00:48:21,857 --> 00:48:24,568
How are you, my treacherous friend?

807
00:48:25,193 --> 00:48:27,237
You seem to look okay.

808
00:48:27,779 --> 00:48:32,784
And, finally, I caught you red-handed.

809
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:37,164
I now have evidence, so, it's obvious.

810
00:48:37,247 --> 00:48:39,374
You can't lie to me anymore.

811
00:48:39,875 --> 00:48:41,084
Traitor!

812
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:43,670
[suspenseful music playing]

813
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:48,634
[Diego] <i>Ivy Aguas is on our side.</i>

814
00:48:48,717 --> 00:48:52,721
<i>She's the reason why</i>
<i>we should keep fighting!</i>

815
00:48:52,804 --> 00:48:54,389
[Julio] <i>I've caught you now.</i>

816
00:48:54,473 --> 00:48:58,560
<i>We set the trap,</i>
<i>and you jumped right into it.</i>

817
00:48:58,644 --> 00:49:00,145
<i>You're a traitor.</i>

818
00:49:00,228 --> 00:49:02,981
<i>And we were right all along.</i>

819
00:49:03,065 --> 00:49:07,944
<i>I won't let any traitors</i>
<i>walk out of here alive.</i>

820
00:49:08,028 --> 00:49:11,406
[Ivy] <i>I'm not done yet, old man!</i>

821
00:49:11,490 --> 00:49:13,992
<i>If Lily was safe,</i>
<i>she would've called by now.</i>

822
00:49:14,076 --> 00:49:16,578
<i>-You think you're tough, huh?</i>
<i>-What are you doing?</i>

823
00:49:16,662 --> 00:49:19,831
[Emilia laughing]

824
00:49:19,915 --> 00:49:22,042
[theme music playing]
